			<div class="content" id="post-content-4442340">
									

<p>I enjoyed this. It was an interesting read. The do gooder morality is in start contrast with what we read about most sarkism, so much so that I wonder about her ignorance based on as you noted her specific teacher despite her seeming expertise. But thats kind of in a different direction than what you'd laid out. And I like articles that aren't all just depressing and dark.</p>
<p>I do agree with other commenters that the hidden text should be unhidden in some way. This doesn't look like it would be a formatscrew and so I did not have and suspicions about it till I read the comments. Maybe a semi-hidden link to an alt list pages portion? Or a link in a footnote? I think something that leaves some sort of visible trail would be helpful.</p>
<p>Also I agree you should either create or commission a more scientific/anatomical picture (or just a skeletal depiction) or just take it out. Some kind of more scientific visual element would help a lot. I think it detracts from the article as is. For example I spent 30 minutes using a couple CC images from the noun project and used GIMP to make this skeletal diagram(<a href="http://scp-sandbox-3.wdfiles.com/local--files/rounzie/4197">http://scp-sandbox-3.wdfiles.com/local--files/rounzie/4197</a>). I think you could have a much better visual with this article without a huge investment in time.</p>

